# Build context of the Crible image (docs/07, section "Docker").
#
# The context must never carry a secret. `.env.prod` holds the production
# accesses (ADR-0032) and it is not versioned: it must not travel to the
# builder either. Every `.env*` file is excluded, the example included, so a
# new file of that family can never leak by omission.
.env*

# Data, models and exchanges live in `data/`, `models/` and `exchange/` and are
# never part of the image (AGENTS.md, rule 14). The image mounts them.
data/
models/
exchange/
target/
.pytest_cache/
*.onnx
*.parquet
*.f16
*.f32
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# The image needs the workspace manifests, `crates/`, `rust-toolchain.toml` and
# `docker/` only.
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.opencode/
.github/
ci/
clients/
tools/
docs/
.claude/runs/
.DS_Store
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
README.md
Makefile
opencode.json
